   "id": 535111,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "How are the formation of urea and uric acid similar and different?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1046954,
     "content_html": "In birds, reptiles, and insects, the urea cycle converts ammonia to urea. In mammals, the uric acid cycle converts ammonia to uric acid. Formation of urea from ammonia requires less energy and is less complex than uric acid formation."
    },
    {
